WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.040
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going&nbsp;
to explain an American horror-thriller film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:15.920
called “13 Sins”. Spoilers ahead!&nbsp;
Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:23.120
The movie begins in Perth Australia. Professor&nbsp;
Edgar Solomon is welcome to make a speech in front&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:29.120
of several people at a party. He recites a kid’s&nbsp;
poem about a rabbit and a bear but the crowd gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:34.720
uncomfortable when the poem gets inappropriate.&nbsp;
He is stopped by a woman beside him who is as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:41.040
surprised as everyone else. Edgar apologizes&nbsp;
and cuts one of her fingers off using a knife.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.320
Her screams make everyone else run away while&nbsp;
the professor collects the finger in a tissue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.920
The security guard asks him to put his hands&nbsp;
up and when he doesn’t oblige, he is shot dead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.880
With his last strength, Edgar tries to get&nbsp;
to his mobile phone but is unsuccessful. 
&nbsp;

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:05.760
Elsewhere, Salesman Elliot Brindle lives in&nbsp;
New Orleans, Louisiana. He and his fiance are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.920
expecting to have a baby soon and are&nbsp;
about to get married in a few days. At&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:15.280
such an important point in his life, Elliot is&nbsp;
told that he is fired. According to his boss,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:23.120
he is too much of an empath to be in sales.&nbsp;
Following that, Elliot goes home to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:28.080
mentally challenged younger brother Michael.&nbsp;
Michael is his biggest responsibility because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.880
he pays twelve hundred dollars monthly for his&nbsp;
outpatient care. Now that he is unemployed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:38.320
Michael is at risk of being sent to a mental&nbsp;
institution that he dreads. After the encounter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:44.480
Elliot drives to his abusive and racist father&nbsp;
Samson to ask for help. However, he finds out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:49.680
that Samson has lost all his retirement funds&nbsp;
and will now have to move with them. 
&nbsp;

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:53.680
At night, Elliot is alone in the&nbsp;
car when he is troubled by a fly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:58.560
He gets a call from someone who claims that he&nbsp;
has been selected for a one-of-a-kind game show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.680
that could make him a lot of money. At first,&nbsp;
Elliot thinks that the person is a scammer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:08.960
He is about to end the call but stops when the&nbsp;
initiator recites all of Elliot’s family history.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:17.040
He seems to know everything significant that has&nbsp;
happened in Elliot’s life since his childhood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:22.160
including the details about his mother’s fatal&nbsp;
car accident. At last, he also talks about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:27.200
fly that has been bothering him recently. Elliot&nbsp;
is left speechless. The man claims that if he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.320
kills the fly, a thousand dollars will be sent&nbsp;
to his bank account. Without thinking much of it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:38.160
Elliot swats the fly and kills it. Seconds later,&nbsp;
a notification informs him that his bank account&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.960
has been credited with a thousand dollars. He&nbsp;
quickly gets out of the car to check if someone is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:48.800
spying on him. Looking around, he realizes that he&nbsp;
is in fact alone, but if that is true there is no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:53.840
way to explain the money in his bank account. 
The person says that his next challenge is to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:59.600
swallow the fly for exactly three thousand six&nbsp;
hundred twenty-two dollars. Elliot quickly gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:04.080
in the car and rushes back home. He checks his&nbsp;
computer and sees that the thousand dollars are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:09.840
still in his account. He is in need of money, and&nbsp;
also wants to check if the initiator is legit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.960
Hence, he eats the dead fly reluctantly. He&nbsp;
yet again gets the phone call from the person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:19.200
congratulating him for completing the second&nbsp;
task. The money is soon transferred to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:25.120
bank account. Confused by all this, Elliot&nbsp;
inquires if he is being watched even in his home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:30.080
The voice says that he can get his privacy back&nbsp;
if he wishes to but that would mean he would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:35.520
disqualified from the game. Following that, he is&nbsp;
briefed about the rules of the game. Elliot will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:40.800
have to complete a series of thirteen challenges,&nbsp;
each of which will result in greater rewards. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:46.080
he fails to complete any of them, interferes in&nbsp;
the game, or reveals the game to anyone else,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:51.040
he will lose all the money, including any he&nbsp;
has already won. Since he has completed two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:56.720
challenges, he has only eleven more left. If he&nbsp;
wants to continue the game, he is asked to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:06.400
“I will dance with the Golden Toad”. Elliot does&nbsp;
as said and is registered as a contestant. 
&nbsp;

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:11.920
The next day, he is in a park with Shelby and her&nbsp;
parents impatiently waiting for the next call.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:17.200
Some minutes later, he is told that the third&nbsp;
challenge for five thousand dollars is to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:23.200
a child cry. He excuses himself and starts looking&nbsp;
for the perfect child. A little girl comes running&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:28.080
to him, giving him the perfect opportunity. He&nbsp;
tells her that her parents are going to leave her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:36.000
in an orphanage and makes her cry. The child runs&nbsp;
to her parents while he receives the cash prize.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:41.040
He quickly gets in the car with Shelby to&nbsp;
drive away as the parents yell curses at him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:46.080
Following that, the pair goes to the church to&nbsp;
pick up Elliot’s father. He gets a call again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:51.360
and is told that for the fourth challenge, he&nbsp;
should burn a nativity scene handcrafted by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:57.120
blind kids for the church. When no one is looking,&nbsp;
Elliot brings the structure outside and burns it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:01.520
The fire accidentally spreads around the&nbsp;
church and gets uncontrollable. He quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:06.800
runs away with his family after ringing the&nbsp;
fire alarm. Moments later, ten thousand dollars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:12.640
is credited to his account. Not long after, he&nbsp;
gets the next challenge and is asked to follow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:17.120
a homeless person by the side of the road.
In the police station, the little girl’s parents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:21.840
have come to report the incident. At the same&nbsp;
time, the homeless person also arrives there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:26.800
Detective Chilcoat is told that someone stole&nbsp;
the homeless person’s clothes and belongings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:30.880
When the sketches of the felon are made, they&nbsp;
realize that the person who stole the clothes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:36.960
burned the church, and troubled the girl is the&nbsp;
same. Elliot is now in challenge six. He is asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:42.400
to take a man from a specific apartment out for&nbsp;
coffee. He believes that the challenge is too easy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:48.640
but he soon realizes the catch. The person he is&nbsp;
taking out is lying dead in the bathtub. With no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:54.400
way out, he sprays a freshener all over the corpse&nbsp;
to hide the smell. He then dresses it and drags it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:59.040
out on a wheelbarrow to the nearest diner. The&nbsp;
waitress comes to take his order and doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:03.840
think much about the dead guy because his face&nbsp;
is hidden with a hat. Elliot is given a deadline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:09.920
to complete the mission, hence the slow waitress&nbsp;
annoys him. Just then, a group of policemen enters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:14.560
the diner for lunch. When the coffee doesn’t&nbsp;
arrive till the last second, Elliot snatches a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:20.240
cup from the policemen’s table. The challenge is&nbsp;
completed but he is in trouble with the police.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:25.360
They ask him to come out to talk but he sees that&nbsp;
they were drinking on duty and calls them out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:31.040
At last, he manages to run away while arguing. 
He gets a call from the initiator who is impressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:36.160
by his skills. Hence, he jumps him directly to&nbsp;
the eighth challenge. But Elliot’s happiness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:41.600
doesn’t last for long when he is informed that&nbsp;
he has left his library card in the diner. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:46.480
police will soon find him but if he completes&nbsp;
all challenges, the initiator will get him free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:52.960
no matter what. Now, his only way to a free life&nbsp;
is to complete the challenges. Following that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:58.560
a van picks Elliot up and brings him somewhere&nbsp;
for his next mission. Back in the diner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:04.400
the policemen find the corpse and start to&nbsp;
investigate. Detective Chilcoat sees a strange man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:09.280
talking to the waitress. The waitress says that&nbsp;
the man was inquiring about Elliot. The detective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:14.400
starts to follow the guy to the trailer and finds&nbsp;
that he has been investigating the game. He has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:20.080
found out where it first started and what happens&nbsp;
to the people who play it. However, no information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:25.760
about the initiator is available. In the meantime,&nbsp;
Elliot is taken to a room where he meets his high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:32.880
school bully John. It turns out his next challenge&nbsp;
is to cut off John’s arm. He doesn’t have to do it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:41.360
forcefully because John is volunteering to get&nbsp;
his arm cut for money. When Elliot hesitates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:46.160
the guy reminds him of all the ways he was&nbsp;
bullied, making him do it. After cutting it off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:51.280
he drives John to the hospital. He gets two&nbsp;
hundred fifty thousand dollars for the mission.
&nbsp;

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:58.560
Then, he drives to his practice dinner for his&nbsp;
wedding. His next mission is to trash the party in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:03.600
front of everyone and urinate in one of the flower&nbsp;
arrangements. The police arrive there looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:09.280
for Michael accusing him of public nudity. Elliot&nbsp;
takes the opportunity to help Michael and distract&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:15.040
the police by trashing the party. He breaks all&nbsp;
the cutleries and pees on the flowers. This way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:19.840
Shelby thinks that he is doing it for his brother&nbsp;
when in reality he is doing it for the challenge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:25.280
He manages to run away from the security but&nbsp;
his next challenge is to surrender himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:30.240
He reluctantly goes back and is arrested. In&nbsp;
the police station, he is interrogated about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:35.120
everything he did throughout the day. When he&nbsp;
is accused of things he didn’t do, he finds out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:40.560
someone else is also playing the games. When no&nbsp;
one is watching, he breaks the bottom of the chair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:46.000
and uses it as a weapon to hold a policeman&nbsp;
hostage. At last, he jumps off the window and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:51.520
lands on a dumpster. He loses his phone in the&nbsp;
chase and has no way to contact the initiator.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:56.960
Just then, he notices a homeless woman walking&nbsp;
by and assumes she is sent by the initiator.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.960 --> 00:09:01.280
The two enter a trailer nearby. 
Somewhere else, Detective Chilcoat finds the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:06.320
conspiracy theorist, Vogler, he was looking for.&nbsp;
It turns out that his wife had played the game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:11.520
some years ago and died while playing it.&nbsp;
Since then, Vogler has been trying to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:16.720
the initiator. Back in the trailer, the woman&nbsp;
asks Elliot to hang a clothes hanger as his next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:22.000
mission. He does it but soon finds out the string&nbsp;
goes across the road that a group of youngsters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:27.440
is riding their bikes on. If the string stays&nbsp;
there, it will cut their heads off. Elliot quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:32.320
removes the string not wanting to kill people&nbsp;
for the challenge. However, the second person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:38.400
who is also playing the game ties another string&nbsp;
across the road and brutally kills the youngsters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:47.120
Seeing their decapitated bodies, Elliot refuses&nbsp;
to continue the game. He runs behind the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:52.960
player to stop him as well. The man gets in a van&nbsp;
and drives away while being followed by Elliot.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:58.400
The initiator calls Elliot on a phone that he had&nbsp;
stolen earlier to tell him about his last mission.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:05.040
He says that the last mission is the same for all&nbsp;
players; he has to kill one of his family. Elliot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:10.080
ignores the call, not wanting to continue the&nbsp;
game. To his surprise, he sees the van parked in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:15.440
front of his apartment building. When he goes in&nbsp;
he finds his father in the living room and Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:21.120
in the bathroom. He puts two and two together and&nbsp;
figures out that the second player is Michael.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:25.920
Michael still wants to play the game and is&nbsp;
ready to shoot their father dead to win it. 
&nbsp;

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:29.520
To their surprise, the father claims&nbsp;
that he had also played the game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:34.960
many years ago. He won after killing their&nbsp;
mother. The brothers are left speechless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:39.600
Elliot gets ready to kill him but the father&nbsp;
cuts his own throat to keep them from winning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:44.800
Elliot wants to end everything but Michael points&nbsp;
his gun at him to win the game. While trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:49.920
make him understand, Elliot accidentally shoots&nbsp;
Michael. Even then, the younger brother doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:55.360
give up. He stabs Elliot but dies in the&nbsp;
process. Elliot has finally completed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.360 --> 00:11:01.040
all thirteen challenges. He limps away from the&nbsp;
house while being watched by Detective Chilcoat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:06.160
We find out that the detective is also working&nbsp;
for the game. He has killed Vogler because he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:12.160
was too close to finding out about the initiator.&nbsp;
Detective Chilcoat goes inside the house to light&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:18.320
Michael and his father’s body on fire to erase the&nbsp;
evidence. Before he can, Elliot arrives there and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:24.320
shoots him dead. In the last scene, he calls&nbsp;
Shelby and tells her he is fine. She informs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:31.040
him of a phone call she received that morning&nbsp;
asking her to eat a fly. Elliot freezes in shock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:36.560
but Shelby says that she declined the offer. 
